   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz7Bo",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I'm standing to champion a party that has the power to truly shake up politics in New Zealand. I was getting increasingly frustrated - like many New Zealanders - with the 3 year political football of big promises, poor delivery, blame the last guys, rinse, repeat. Opportunity represents a fresh take on politics. Pragmatic, not dogmatic. Sensible, not tribal. Future focused for all New Zealanders. I'm standing as a candidate to fight for the future."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz7Dz",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "First and foremost - I'm a party vote only candidate. I absolutely believe I have the values, skills, and work ethic to represent my community - but for now I'm putting my all into supporting The Opportunity Party to maximise their party vote. At 33 on the list, this election is me putting my time and effort behind a party I truly believe will help Kiwis thrive, with or without me. Party vote Opportunity."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz7GA",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Make our tax system more modern by taxing work less and taxing land fairly."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz7IL",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Build an infrastructure plan that will future proof our region, not just fix what's broken."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoz7KW",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Make energy abundance a national priority to ease the cost of living and protect our power grid."
     }
    ],
